\par\par \uc2 Best Colleges of India 2026\par \b \uc2 Fashion Design  The style vanguard  \uc2 National Institute of Fashion Technology\uc2 , New Delhi\b0\par\par\uc2 Shelly Anand \par \uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2026\par \uc2 India Today\par \uc2 INTY\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2026. Living Media India Ltd \par \par \uc2 The flagship \uc2 NIFT\uc2  campus remains at the forefront of design education in the country, promoting industry partnerships and mentor programmes to hold the bar high\par \par \uc2 As the fashion industry undergoes rapid transformation, the \uc2 National Institute of Fashion Technology (NIFT)\uc2  Delhi is preparing students for a future in which creativity and technology go hand-in-hand. A major focus this year will be the integration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Artificial Intelligence\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the curriculum, enabling students to use advanced tools for trend analysis, forecasting, design innovation, research and sustainable fashion practices.\par \par \uc2 For NIFT Delhi, AI is not a substitute for creativity but a catalyst for it. "The biggest game changer would be its incorporation into the fashion design curriculum," says Professor Shinju Mahajan, campus director, NIFT Delhi. "This is our first priority and has been brainstormed intensively." The challenge, she says, lies in deciding when students should be introduced to AI as a design and research tool. If unrestricted access is given from the first year, there is a risk that design sensibilities may not fully develop, "blurring the distinction between a layperson using AI and a professional designer applying it with expertise".\par \par \uc2 Fashion design, says Tanu Kashyap, director general-NIFT, remains \uc2 NIFT\uc2 's flagship programme and, for over 40 years, has shaped generations of successful designers and professionals. "We continue to set the standards that inspire design schools across India and reassert NIFT Delhi's position as the undisputed leader in fashion education," she says.\par \par \uc2 Industry engagement is another one of the institute's defining strengths. Beyond placements, students benefit from regular interactions with industry leaders through lectures, projects and sessions that expose them to real-world challenges and opportunities.\par \par \uc2 A recent initiative is its student-driven placement cell. Senior students play an active role in engaging with industry partners, reaching out to organisations and creating opportunities for internships and placements. The student-led entrepreneurship cell, on the other hand, encourages innovation through case-study competitions, collaborative projects and industry-linked initiatives. The NIFT Foundation for Design Innovation Incubation Cell will also help here, giving students a structured platform to develop business ideas and entrepreneurial ventures.\par \par \uc2 NIFT Delhi also plans to introduce a dedicated student media team in 2026 that will manage social media engagement and public relations initiatives for the campus, giving students valuable experience in communication, storytelling and brand management.\par \par \uc2 Creating a supportive campus is a priority. At the heart of this effort is NIFT Delhi's academic mentoring system, under which faculty guides small groups of students throughout their academic journey. A popular elective on gender sensitisation has also been introduced to encourage acceptance, respect and awareness across the student community.\par \par \uc2 Document INTY000020260629em760000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw117\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1755\pichgoal600
